---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/open-v2.css';
---

<Layout
  title="M221Tech Open | Public datasets & reports from Senegal"
  description="Explore selected public datasets and focused reports from M221Tech, with clear boundaries between open outputs and internal methods."
>
  <div class="m221-open-page">
    <section class="m221-open-hero">
      <div class="m221-container m221-open-hero-inner">
        <a class="m221-open-breadcrumb" href="/#open">← M221Tech / Open</a>
        <span class="m221-open-kicker">M221TECH / OPEN</span>
        <h1>Some data is better when it travels.</h1>
        <p class="m221-open-lead">Selected datasets go public when they are solid enough to reuse. Questions that need more context can become focused reports.</p>
        <div class="m221-open-actions">
          <a class="is-primary" href="https://www.kaggle.com/m221tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browse public data ↗</a>
          <a class="is-secondary" href="#datasets">See how Open works ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="m221-open-local-wrap">
      <nav class="m221-container m221-open-local-nav" aria-label="Open navigation" data-open-nav>
        <a href="#datasets" data-open-link="datasets"><span>01</span>Datasets</a>
        <a href="#reports" data-open-link="reports"><span>02</span>Reports</a>
        <a href="#boundary" data-open-link="boundary"><span>03</span>Scope</a>
        <a href="#contact" data-open-link="contact"><span>04</span>Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <section class="m221-open-chapter" id="datasets" data-open-section>
      <div class="m221-container">
        <header class="m221-open-chapter-head">
          <div class="m221-open-index">01 / DATASETS</div>
          <h2>Public when it is ready.</h2>
          <p>Open does not mean dumping everything. We publish selected datasets when the structure, documentation and context are good enough to be useful outside M221Tech.</p>
        </header>

        <article class="m221-open-dataset">
          <div class="m221-open-dataset-main">
            <span class="m221-open-eyebrow">PUBLIC DATA / SELECTED RELEASES</span>
            <h3>M221Tech datasets</h3>
            <p>Reusable data from the fields we work on, released selectively rather than by default. Public datasets are shared through the M221Tech Kaggle space.</p>
            <div class="m221-open-dataset-actions">
              <a class="is-open" href="https://www.kaggle.com/m221tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Kaggle ↗</a>
              <a class="is-domain" href="https://www.kaggle.com/m221tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">kaggle.com/m221tech</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="m221-open-dataset-meta" aria-label="Public dataset principles">
            <div class="m221-open-meta-row"><span>Selection</span><strong>Not every internal dataset</strong></div>
            <div class="m221-open-meta-row"><span>Quality</span><strong>Structured before release</strong></div>
            <div class="m221-open-meta-row"><span>Context</span><strong>Documented enough to reuse</strong></div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="m221-open-chapter is-alt" id="reports" data-open-section>
      <div class="m221-container">
        <header class="m221-open-chapter-head">
          <div class="m221-open-index">02 / REPORTS</div>
          <h2>A question first. A report second.</h2>
          <p>Reports are not a shelf of generic PDFs. They start with a concrete question and use the data and context M221Tech already knows how to work with.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="m221-open-report-grid">
          <article class="m221-open-report-step">
            <span>01 / QUESTION</span>
            <h3>Start with what you want to understand.</h3>
            <p>A competition, a category, a product set, a trend or another question connected to data we cover.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="m221-open-report-step">
            <span>02 / SCOPE</span>
            <h3>Check what the data can actually support.</h3>
            <p>We define the useful perimeter before promising an answer the underlying data cannot carry.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="m221-open-report-step">
            <span>03 / OUTPUT</span>
            <h3>Build the answer around the question.</h3>
            <p>The result can be a focused analysis, a structured extract or another useful format depending on the need.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="m221-open-report-cta">
          <div>
            <h3>Have a question worth digging into?</h3>
            <p>Send the question and a little context. We will tell you whether it fits the data we currently cover.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="mailto:m221tech@gmail.com?subject=M221Tech%20report%20request">Request a report →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="m221-open-chapter" id="boundary" data-open-section>
      <div class="m221-container">
        <header class="m221-open-chapter-head">
          <div class="m221-open-index">03 / SCOPE</div>
          <h2>Open data. Not open everything.</h2>
          <p>The public layer is deliberate. M221Tech can share useful data without publishing every internal method, pipeline or working database behind it.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="m221-open-boundary">
          <article>
            <span>PUBLIC</span>
            <h3>Selected datasets.</h3>
            <p>Datasets chosen for reuse when they are mature enough to stand on their own.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>ON REQUEST</span>
            <h3>Focused analysis.</h3>
            <p>Reports and extracts can be shaped around a specific question when the available data supports it.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>IN-HOUSE</span>
            <h3>Methods and pipelines.</h3>
            <p>Collection workflows, transformation logic and internal tooling remain part of how M221Tech builds its products.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="m221-open-contact" id="contact" data-open-section>
      <div class="m221-container m221-open-contact-inner">
        <div class="m221-open-index">04 / CONTACT</div>
        <div>
          <h2>Dataset, question or idea?</h2>
          <p>Tell us what you are trying to understand or reuse.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:m221tech@gmail.com?subject=M221Tech%20Open">m221tech@gmail.com →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const header = document.querySelector('.m221-header');
    const localWrap = document.querySelector('.m221-open-local-wrap');
    const links = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[data-open-link]'));
    const sections = links
      .map((link) => document.getElementById(link.dataset.openLink || ''))
      .filter(Boolean);

    let activeId = '';
    let targetId = null;
    let ticking = false;

    const offset = () => (header?.offsetHeight || 0) + (localWrap?.offsetHeight || 0) + 1;

    const setActive = (id) => {
      if (!id || activeId === id) return;
      activeId = id;
      links.forEach((link) => {
        if (link.dataset.openLink === id) link.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
        else link.removeAttribute('aria-current');
      });
    };

    const currentSection = () => {
      const marker = offset() + 8;
      let current = sections[0];
      for (const section of sections) {
        if (section.getBoundingClientRect().top <= marker) current = section;
        else break;
      }
      const atBottom = window.innerHeight + window.scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 3;
      return atBottom ? sections[sections.length - 1] : current;
    };

    const sync = () => {
      ticking = false;
      if (!sections.length) return;
      if (targetId) {
        const target = document.getElementById(targetId);
        if (target) {
          setActive(targetId);
          if (Math.abs(target.getBoundingClientRect().top - offset()) > 3) return;
        }
        targetId = null;
      }
      setActive(currentSection()?.id);
    };

    const schedule = () => {
      if (ticking) return;
      ticking = true;
      requestAnimationFrame(sync);
    };

    links.forEach((link) => {
      link.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
        const id = link.dataset.openLink;
        const target = id ? document.getElementById(id) : null;
        if (!target) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        targetId = id;
        setActive(id);
        const top = Math.max(0, target.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY - offset());
        const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        window.scrollTo({ top, behavior: reduceMotion ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
        history.replaceState(null, '', `#${id}`);
      });
    });

    const release = () => {
      targetId = null;
      schedule();
    };

    window.addEventListener('scroll', schedule, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', schedule, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('wheel', release, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('touchstart', release, { passive: true });

    requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      if (location.hash) {
        const id = location.hash.slice(1);
        const target = document.getElementById(id);
        if (target && links.some((link) => link.dataset.openLink === id)) {
          window.scrollTo({ top: Math.max(0, target.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY - offset()), behavior: 'auto' });
        }
      }
      sync();
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
